  "title": "Kueper2024: Unilateral vs bilateral movement-execution EEG dataset",
  "description": "This dataset contains EEG recordings from 8 healthy participants performing self-initiated, self-paced reaching movements in two conditions: unilateral (right arm) and bilateral (both arms). Data were recorded with a 64-channel wireless active-electrode system at 500 Hz. The dataset supports research on movement intention recognition for exoskeleton-supported stroke rehabilitation.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a Brain Products LiveAmp64 and Acticap slim active electrodes (extended 10-20 montage, FCz reference, AFz ground, 500 Hz sampling, amplifier prefiltered at 0.1-131 Hz). Each participant performed 3 sets of 40 self-initiated movements per condition (unilateral and bilateral), giving 6 runs per subject.",
